Z||000000||RossT||12-22-1999||04:38 AM||||I have been reading this forum for about 8 months now, and it seems that many of you(us)<BR>carry a scanner in our fiero(s). Not wanting to be out in the cold trying to count blinking dash lights, I started looking for a<BR>cheap trouble code scanner that can be left in the car without worring about it being stolen.  I finally bought  a Innovar GM trouble code scanner for a grand total of $13.00 (plus shipping).  It may not be the best, but for that price I don't have to worry about it.<P>go to yahoo.com<BR>click on auctions<BR>search for fiero<BR>about a dozen items will come up<BR>scoll down to bottom of the list and you will find related items. <BR>some guy in Texas has alot of them, he keeps posting them as they sell.<P>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000001||Patrick||12-22-1999||04:48 AM||||<BR>I've never really had a problem counting the flashes from the light in the dash myself. The paperclip I use to short the ALCL connection cost me nothing, so I never have to worry about losing it or having it stolen! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||RossT||12-22-1999||05:03 AM||||Good point!! Just don't poke yourself..One nice thing about the scanner is that you can use it on many other gm/saturn cars. save your friends and family bucks before thier cars go into the shop. ok I guess that one could carry a bunch of paper clips..<P>Ross||||reg||1
